=== 2026-09-06, the original noise arm's position-collapse gate, run standalone ===
No state was rebuilt and no model was loaded: output/states.npz and
output/states_meta.json are untouched by this run and still hold what the
2026-09-05 build wrote. What ran is the new gate alone, over the committed
original-noise record, invoked as `python3 build_states.py
--check-nullold-collapse`, which reads that record and exits before the model
load. It exists because the fifth review of pull request 84 found that the state
builder measured position collapse on the first five of the arm's 125 trials,
logged the numbers without enforcing them, and then rebuilt all 125 by repeating
each trial's last-position vector, so seventeen of the eighteen null-basin
representatives hypothesis H6 is scored on came from trials that had never been
measured. All 125 now pass, with two orders of magnitude of room against both
tolerances, and so do all eighteen representatives. The gate is a hard stop
inside build_states.py from now on, which means a future rebuild refuses to tile
a trial that is not position-collapsed rather than logging it. Wall clock 3.1
seconds. Recorded as deviation 15 in RESULTS_EXP011.md.
